                <pb facs="0241" n="148" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg148"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.34119/194: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Weddell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-09-24T16:00:00-04:00">September 24, 1935—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>216. From Dawson. Paragraph number 3, my 209, September 18, 10 p.m. Bolivian
                    delegation has orally informed Prisoners of War Committee that the Bolivian
                    Government does not feel that it is necessary to take action on the proposal for
                    the exchange of disabled prisoners “in view of the short time remaining before
                    the Conference declares the war at an end after which all prisoners should
                    automatically be released.” [Dawson.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Weddell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
